# Lakebase project – common ignores
.env
application-local.properties
.tmp/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Consort per-run observability (NOT planning corpus): the agent event log + the
# resolved run-config snapshot are local to a single run/feature drive and are
# re-initialized each run, so they must never enter git history (a stray
# `git add -A` from a build commit would otherwise carry one feature's log onto
# the next branch). The committed .consort corpus (features/, planning/, sprints/,
# workflow-state.json, product-overview.md, nfrs.md, design/) is unaffected. The
# legacy roots (.sftdd/.tdd) are kept for projects created before the rename.
.consort/agent-log.jsonl
.consort/run-config.json
.consort/drive-live.log
# The detached drive's live pid file (consort-drive --detach writes it, consort-watch reads it).
# Per-run scratch; an untracked drive.pid otherwise re-dirties the tree and re-blocks the next
# experiment cut's clean-tree check.
.consort/drive.pid
.consort/diagnostics/
# next.json is the drive's stop-state pointer, rewritten on EVERY stop. Committing it dirties the
# tree on the next stop and re-blocks the experiment cut's clean-tree check , it is per-run state,
# not corpus, so it never enters history.
.consort/next.json
# The build lane's TRANSIENT run-state: per-cycle records (cycles/), per-experiment scratch
# (experiments/), and the live build-pipeline pointer (pipeline.json). These churn every cycle and
# describe the mechanics of a single run, not the design corpus, so they are gitignored the same way
# next.json is , otherwise their per-cycle churn re-dirties the tree and re-blocks the next
# experiment cut. The DESIGN corpus (features/, planning/, sprints/, workflow-state.json,
# product-overview.md, nfrs.md, design/, architecture/) is committed, not ignored (Consort persists
# it on the feature branch at each cut so the spec history survives for later stories).
.consort/cycles/
.consort/experiments/
.consort/pipeline.json
# NOTE: the PER-FEATURE ledger .consort/features/<id>/pipeline.json is deliberately NOT ignored —
# it is the durable per-story pipeline state (persisted on the feature branch so it survives across
# sessions). Ignoring it lost the ledger. A promotion-merge conflict on it is resolved at the MERGE
# layer (scm-merge reconciles it to the run side), never by untracking it.
# The turn recorder's per-run observability: its internal file-hash map
# (.recorder-state.json, used for delta computation), the routing-decision
# diagnostic stream (routing-decisions.jsonl), and the per-turn record dirs
# (turns/). All three are re-created every run and describe a single run's
# mechanics, not the design corpus (the curated replay corpus lives in the kit
# repo, never in a scaffolded project). The recorder already treats them as
# internal; ignore them here so a corpus commit never sweeps them into history
# and an untracked one never blocks the experiment / feature-branch fork's
# clean-tree check.
.consort/.recorder-state.json
.consort/routing-decisions.jsonl
.consort/turns/
# Playwright-MCP's browser scratch (screenshots/traces a UX/review turn drops). Transient
# tool output, not corpus; ignore it so it never dirties the tree before an experiment cut.
.playwright-mcp/
.sftdd/agent-log.jsonl
.sftdd/run-config.json
.tdd/agent-log.jsonl
.tdd/run-config.json

# The RUN PINs: WORKSPACE-local, checkout-proof overrides of the committed
# `.lakebase/kit-ref` (Consort kit) and `.lakebase/scm-utils-ref` (substrate). The
# drive writes them at launch to pin the run's versions for the whole run; they
# MUST stay gitignored so a branch checkout/reset (which forks from
# origin/<parent>) can never restore a branch-committed ref out from under the run
# and silently execute the wrong version. The committed `.lakebase/kit-ref` and
# `.lakebase/scm-utils-ref` stay tracked (CI resolves KIT_REF / SCM_UTILS_REF from
# them).
.lakebase/kit-ref.local
.lakebase/scm-utils-ref.local

# The runtime SCM CLAIM state: per working tree, rewritten by every SCM transition
# (claim / pr-ready / ci-green / merged). If it is git-tracked, a branch checkout
# or `git reset --hard origin/<tier>` restores a branch-COMMITTED stale claim over
# the live one, and the next feature's claim then refuses "already-claimed-other"
# until a manual abandon+reclaim (issue #203 / Finding 28). Never track it; the
# committed kit-ref / scm-utils-ref pins above stay tracked deliberately.
.lakebase/workflow-state.json

# Per-agent local memory: each role subagent (memory: project) persists its own
# learnings here mid-run. It is local + churny (re-written every run), not feature
# code, so it must never be committed nor count as a dirty working tree , an
# untracked .claude/agent-memory/ otherwise blocks the experiment-branch fork
# (assertCleanForFork) the moment a role saves a memory.
.claude/agent-memory/

# Unrelated agent tooling writes a local .isaac/ config dir. It is not project
# source and churns per run; the experiment-cut guard already tolerates it by
# name, so ignore it here too so it never enters git nor blocks a fork on a kit
# whose clean-tree check still counts untracked files.
.isaac/
